   "text": "What is ES6?"
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "ES6 stands for ECMAScript 6."
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "ECMAScript was created to standardize JavaScript, and ES6 is the 6th version\nof ECMAScript, it was published in 2015, and is also known as ECMAScript 2015."
  },
  {
   "type": "h2",
   "text": "Why Should I Learn ES6?"
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "React uses ES6, and you should be familiar with some of the new features\nlike:"
  },
  {
   "type": "list",
   "ordered": false,
   "items": [
    "Classes",
    "Arrow Functions",
    "Variables (let, const, var)",
